# Issue #1087 (milestone 3, C6/C9 end-to-end): the two_way_clean scenario with `transport ice`: the call is set up through
# the full stack (offer/answer, trickled candidates, ICE, DTLS) and its media goes as SRTP over the bundled transport
# on the same links. Its expect lines are two_way_clean's; the setup.* and transport.* lines check the connection.
# sm_compare runs the direct twin; this copy is not compared (`compare off`).

name ice_two_way_clean
describe Two-way audio call (user <-> AI) on a clean 2.5 Mbps link each way, 25 ms one-way: both directions flawless (#746) -- through ICE, DTLS-SRTP and SDP (transport ice, #1087)
transport ice
compare off
duration 30s
call two-way
video off
at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=25ms queue=300ms
reverse at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=25ms queue=300ms
# The audio lines of clean_link, for each direction.
expect up.audio.concealed_pct < 1
expect up.audio.interruptions == 0
expect down.audio.concealed_pct < 1
expect down.audio.interruptions == 0
expect setup.connected == 1
expect transport.send_failures == 0
